ource arXiv:2407.14358\nPublication type Preprint\nPrimary research role Foundations & surveys\nResearch roles Foundations & surveys Build & maintain\nResearch topics Role: foundation Role: build Foundational methods and concepts\nOriginal publication Original publication https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.14358 \nPDF PDF https://arxiv.org/pdf/2407.14358 \narXiv ID 2407.14358\nDOI 10.48550/arxiv.2407.14358\nRelated resources Stable Audio Open 1.0 /resources/stable-audio-open/ \nBibliographic sources Primary publication https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.14358 \nClassification context Editorial roles and topics follow the publication’s scope as discussed in GameMap. Foundations denotes a general method or component, rather than a game-specific system.\nCode availability Open-source code\nRepositories & licenses Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools (implementation) Repository https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools Implementation scope Research implementation License status Open-source license Code license MIT License License source https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools/blob/main/LICENSE\nProject pages Project homepage https://stability-ai.github.io/stable-audio-open-demo/ \nDemos & setup Run the local audio interface Demo / setup instructions https://github.com/Stability-AI/stable-audio-tools#readme Experience type Documented local run Access conditions Local setup required Usage notes Install the Gradio UI extras and obtain Stable Audio Open weights; accepting model terms and sharing contact details are required.\nPractical use notes MIT covers stable-audio-tools code; Stable Audio Open weights are separately gated by the model community license and require accepting terms/sharing contact details. The project sample page contains audio recordings, not a hosted generator. The project’s demo page is a static audio-sample gallery, not an interactive model demo.\nArtifact review Review status Source reviewed Last checked 2026-10-20\nCode, project & demo evidence Orig