 https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond/blob/main/LICENSE\nProject pages Project homepage https://diamond-wm.github.io \nDemos & setup Play the pretrained world model locally Demo / setup instructions https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond#readme Experience type Documented local run Access conditions Local setup required Usage notes Python, pretrained checkpoints and a compatible CUDA GPU are required; Atari and CS:GO use different documented setups.\nPractical use notes MIT-licensed source and pretrained playable Atari/CS:GO world models are linked. Local interaction needs Python/model dependencies and a CUDA GPU; the project reports approximately 10 FPS on an RTX 3090 for the CS:GO setup. The external hosted link was reachable, but its execution was not independently playtested. A repository mentioning this paper was found through paper metadata, but author ownership or an official project-to-code link was not established. It is not counted as official source code. A project-linked demo endpoint was found, but a working interactive application was not established.\nArtifact review Review status Source reviewed Last checked 2026-10-20\nCode, project & demo evidence Original publication reviewed https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12399  Author project page reviewed https://diamond-wm.github.io  Author-associated repository reviewed https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond  Repository license text inspected https://github.com/eloialonso/diamond/blob/main/LICENSE  Live artifact endpoint checked https://next.journee.ai/demo00001  Survey authors’ official resource mapping https://github.com/Eurekaleo/awesome-ai-for-games/blob/main/data/official-resources.json ","Conference paper cited as reference [9] in AI for Games in the Foundation Model Era. In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024.","Eloi Alonso, Adam Jelley, Vincent Micheli, Anssi Kanervisto, Amos Storkey, Tim Pearce, and François Fleuret","In Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems, 2024.",[514,599