 run Access conditions Local setup required Usage notes Use the Matrix-Game-2 directory rather than the root README, which now documents 4.0. The 2.0 README supplies installation, checkpoint-download and inference/streaming commands. It requires an Nvidia GPU with at least 24 GB memory, compatible PyTorch/FlashAttention and separate model checkpoints. The README specifies MIT; its local LICENSE target is absent, while the repository-root MIT license is available. No local inference was executed.\nPractical use notes Use the Matrix-Game-2 directory rather than the root README, which now documents 4.0. The 2.0 README supplies installation, checkpoint-download and inference/streaming commands. It requires an Nvidia GPU with at least 24 GB memory, compatible PyTorch/FlashAttention and separate model checkpoints. The README specifies MIT; its local LICENSE target is absent, while the repository-root MIT license is available. No local inference was executed.\nArtifact review Review status Source reviewed Last checked 2026-10-20\nCode, project & demo evidence Original paper and author comments https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.13009  Survey authors’ official resource mapping https://github.com/Eurekaleo/awesome-ai-for-games/blob/main/data/official-resources.json  Project homepage https://matrix-game-v2.github.io/  Source repository https://github.com/SkyworkAI/Matrix-Game  Repository license https://github.com/SkyworkAI/Matrix-Game/blob/main/LICENSE  Published implementation files https://github.com/SkyworkAI/Matrix-Game/tree/main/Matrix-Game-2  Version-specific setup https://github.com/SkyworkAI/Matrix-Game/blob/main/Matrix-Game-2/README.md#quick-start  Version documentation reviewed https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SkyworkAI/Matrix-Game/main/Matrix-Game-2/README.md  Version documentation reviewed https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SkyworkAI/Matrix-Game/main/LICENSE ","Preprint cited as reference [127] in AI for Games in the Foundation Model Era. arXiv preprint arXiv:2508.13009,